{"name":"Nighthawks","hex":"#234c47","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nighthawks","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of nighthawk"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nighthawks"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nighthawks (Hopper)","blocks":[{"text":"Nighthawks is a 1942 oil on canvas painting by the American artist Edward Hopper that portrays four people in a downtown diner late at night, as viewed through the diner's large glass window. The light coming from the diner illuminates a darkened and deserted urban streetscape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Nighthawks_by_Edward_Hopper_1942.jpg/330px-Nighthawks_by_Edward_Hopper_1942.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nighthawks_(Hopper)","wikidata":"Q83872"},{"title":"Nighthawk (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Nighthawk is the fourteenth novel in the NUMA Files series by Clive Cussler."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f7/Nighthawk_%28Cussler_novel%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nighthawk_(novel)","wikidata":"Q55625233"},{"title":"Nighthawks (1981 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Nighthawks is a 1981 American neo-noir action thriller film directed by Bruce Malmuth in his solo directorial debut, from a screenplay by David Shaber, based on a story by Shaber and Paul Sylbert. It stars Sylvester Stallone and Billy Dee Williams, with Lindsay Wagner, Persis Khambatta, Nigel Davenport and Rutger Hauer in his American film debut. Its score was composed by Keith Emerson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/50/Nighthawks_movie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nighthawks_(1981_film)","wikidata":"Q1535201"},{"title":"Nighthawks (Nighthawks album)","blocks":[{"text":"Nighthawks is the only studio album by American hip-hop duo Nighthawks, which consisted of rappers Cage and Camu Tao. It was released on November 26, 2002, under Eastern Conference Records. The album is a rap opera concept album."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/19/Nighthawkscamu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nighthawks_(Nighthawks_album)","wikidata":"Q30598157"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Nighthawks_invoice_Ed_Hopper_1942.jpg/500px-Nighthawks_invoice_Ed_Hopper_1942.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Nighthawks_invoice_Ed_Hopper_1942.jpg/500px-Nighthawks_invoice_Ed_Hopper_1942.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Invoice showing $1,971 (equivalent to $38,840 in 2025) going to the artist after commission and costs","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANighthawks_invoice_Ed_Hopper_1942.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/%22Night_Hawks%22_in_the_Art_Institute_of_Chicago.jpg/500px-%22Night_Hawks%22_in_the_Art_Institute_of_Chicago.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/%22Night_Hawks%22_in_the_Art_Institute_of_Chicago.jpg/1280px-%22Night_Hawks%22_in_the_Art_Institute_of_Chicago.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/%22Night_Hawks%22_in_the_Art_Institute_of_Chicago.jpg/500px-%22Night_Hawks%22_in_the_Art_Institute_of_Chicago.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nighthawks in the Art Institute of Chicago (2016)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%22Night_Hawks%22_in_the_Ar